# Application Knowledge Maintenance (opt-in)

If this app has \`app-knowledge.config.json\`, it owns a version-specific knowledge contract for its private in-app assistant. The toolkit is globally installed; never clone it per project.

Before closing a material change to API, user-visible behavior, roles, domain fields, status transitions, UI workflows or assistant tool capabilities:

1. Inspect changed behavior and dependent knowledge documents.
2. Update affected docs and SHA hashes, or document a concrete no-behavior-change decision in the manifest.
3. Revalidate OpenAPI operationId coverage and direct code/test evidence.
4. Run \`app-knowledge.mjs validate\` and \`diff-check\` locally.

Missing/invalid OpenAPI is a **hard stop**, not permission to invent an API specification. Publishing is **never automatic**, only via \`/app-knowledge-publish\`. Dynamic user data and live operations remain inside app-owned tools and backend authorization.

This Rule is advisory. The installed local Git hook provides mechanical commit enforcement once an application opts in.
